---------- Forwarded message ---------
From: clasy...@gmail.com <Unknown>
Date: Monday, September 18, 2017 at 7:21:19 AM UTC-5
Subject: P?S/8 releases past the initial release of PEPS
To: pepswin <Unknown>


Once I get the initial release out the door [legally safe enough!  
Documentation will be in a "beta +" status, still desiring feedback in the 
form of constructive criticism and suggestions], there will be the need to 
have some announcement [either her, or perhaps a designated archive of 
addendums past the release].


The case in point that triggers this:


Because of needs of real-world users, I hope to soon have a working P?S/8 
for RX01 and perhaps TD8E [first without the MR8E-C ROM; there are bugs in 
the version for use with the ROM, contained but not finalized] that should 
be available very soon [time frame in several weeks perhaps].

Thus, there will be a need to add images to the PEPS package but not for 
the purpose of an entire release.  Thus, let's discuss how this should be 
accomplished.

Generally, something like this in PEPS/SIMH requires an Icon/shortcut on 
the Command Window [perhaps two] to launch it and of course the SIMH config 
files should have an independent file with different aims than the release 
one for P?S/8 on TC01/08 DECtape [which is far more functional because a) 
TD8E only get two drives, b) RX01 only get 2 or may 4 drives [two in SIMH] 
and the capacity is far, far, far smaller.  [Note, PEPS uses a build of 
SIMH that supports "fantasy" DECtapes of lengths beyond real-word and 
real-word +, which was a secondary standard quite a few people used because 
the media could often support it, just not all tapes] so that, with slight 
command option restriction, P?S/8 and OS/8 can work with 4096 block 
DECtapes, not the historical smaller values of 2702 octal [standard] and 
3300 octal [extended if you can].  [That's block 0000-7777 octal!].  Thus, 
an RX01 is not all that useful.  But it will be quite "real" and easily 
imaged to SIMH.  The TD8E will be behind this because it involves working 
with recently "unearthed" source code while the RX01 is just one of the 
standard support formats in the main-line source files.  [A long story, but 
a few versions got "orphaned" etc.]  Eventually, I will be bringing out 
also at least one of the four variant RK8E systems:

1) 8 logical units on a single RK05 cartridge booted to drive 0,1,2, or 3.

2) 4 logical units on two  RK05 cartridges.  Can boot to say drive 0 or 1 
OR to drive 2 or 3.  [But not any other combination].  This system is one 
of the more "intercompatible" variants in terms of ease of file conversion 
from/to OS/8, etc.

3) 4 logical drives on four cartridges.  This matches exactly the way OS/8 
addresses RK8E/RK05.  Any logical drive can be booted to.  [Yes, any!]

4) This is the "wave of the future":  P?S/8 on 8 cartridges of the RKS8E 
and the first four if you only have an RK8E.  [The SIMH does not presently 
support the RKS8E.  It's hard for OS/8 to handle it and what was ever done 
is kludgy and arguably dangerous, you can spoof your own cartridges and 
write on what was not intended.  The OS/8 couput is, well no one told you 
to include are idiot handlers, did you expect them to be safe to use?]

This means that each RK05 cartridge supports the entire pack, unlike OS/8 
which need an "A" side and a "B" side.  You get the full capacity; in terms 
of 128 word blocks, this means 31300 blocks [00000-31277].  Will be the 
system of choice with the P?S/8 SHELL [in terms of what SIMH does 
presently].  This will be the "proving ground" for the slow obsolescence 
process that culminates in "retiring" OS/8.  Expect a familiar system, but 
none of the problems [such as inadequate directory, inadequate file names, 
inadequte date support, etc.].  Presently, this is just a small edit from 
the other 3) all of which are available.  [The basic system can only 
address blocks 00000-07777 on every pack.]

P?S/8 for the TC01/08 only requires 4K [but can use all of the rest if 
available].  All of the ones discussed here require a minimum of 8K [and in 
general, this is the usual reason that OS/8 needs 12K.  The RK8E system 
requires more memory to be able to efficiently address the RK05 physical 
record to the nearest 1/2 logical  block of 128 words.  The handler does 
some "dark grey magic" to get around the hardware restrictions.]

Thus, clearly there will be the need for some post-release appendages.  
Please suggest how best this should be done.

For myself, I can upload to Ibiblio.org in some pubic-ally accessed 
directory [read only to you] and make announcements here as well as readme 
files on the ibiblio site, etc.

Speak now or forever hold your PDP-8!

cjl



